# AGILE METHODS:

Agile methods encompass a group of software development methodologies based on iterative development, 
where requirements and solutions evolve through collaboration between self-organizing cross-functional 
teams. Agile promotes flexible responses to change, continuous improvement, and the delivery of 
high-quality software in short, manageable iterations. Key principles include customer collaboration, 
adaptive planning, early and continuous delivery, and a strong focus on individuals and interactions 
over processes and tools.

In agile methods, we focus on: 
	Changing Market Needs 
	End-User Needs 
	Competitive Threats 

The assumptions that we address involve: 
	How are the priorities of the customers going to change over time. 
	The extent/amount of design that we need to put in before coding and testing 
	Planning of all engineering activites.

Progress or no progress (adaptable he) 

Its also incremental: 
	Customer Feeback
	Portion of an Operational System 

Agile Manifesto: 
	Concentrate on responding to change rather then creating a plan and then following it (chaordic). 
	Value individuals and their interaction over process and tools.
	Prefer to invest time in the fking product instead of in documentation. 
	Focus on customer collaboration rather than contract negotiation.

## SCRUMS: 

Type of an agile method which is quick, adaptive, and self organizing. This involves working in 
**SPRINTS** (discussed further on). Scrums focus on specifically on the team level, team exerts complete 
control over the team organizaiton and work processes.

It uses a backlog of the users requirements which is used to choose the work to be done during a Scrum project. 

### SCRUM ORGANIZATION: 

> Product Owner
	> Scrum Master
		> Scrum Team(s) 

a) The client stakeholder for which the system is being built for, maintains the product backlog list 
and priorities. b) He is in charge of the Scrum project, leads the meetings, assesses responses. c) The 
teams are a small group developers who set their own goals and distribute the work among themselves.

### SPRINT: 
 > THE BASIC WORK PROCESS IN SCRUMS
it is a time controlled mini project 
it is normally a 30 day time box with specific tasks  or goals that are to be achieved in that window. 
Begins with a one-day planning session. 
Has a short daily meeting to discuss progress 
Ends with a final half day review
